<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-emiliania-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Emiliania huxleyi Holocene Turing wavelength at 5.808 nm (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 89.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the 5.808 nm Holocene law (0 Ma). Tangential-Sobel annulus on the real SEM peaks at harmonic 30 (spoke score 5.20, centre [192, 168]), and that count textures the shields. Selection-band Pearson r = 0.9944, RMSE = 0.0182. Damped-wing RMSE, integrated at dt = 0.006, is 0.0629. GIF is 12 frames at 720x540. CV similarity against the specimen is 92.6. Foreground fraction 0.675 (specimen) versus 0.435 (simulation); those values are not copies of each other. Overall 89.1/100 (faithfulness 89.0, reproducibility 89.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-emiliania-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 3694038 B, 720×540 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 c90f6524d06e8f07e81b20c7b2d4f9eee909c6aa048c4f0038497905019d3692 (sha256 c90f6524d06e8f07e81b20c7b2d4f9eee909c6aa048c4f0038497905019d3692), spec_fingerprint ccb36351ddf24d5f1022c17c85f5291551afc2f963515079e7b0ebff6253d163. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ccb36351ddf24d5f1022c17c85f5291551afc2f963515079e7b0ebff6253d163; artifact_sha256: c90f6524d06e8f07e81b20c7b2d4f9eee909c6aa048c4f0038497905019d3692; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/emiliania_huxleyi_coccosphere_coccolith.jpg=94d4b431c4912727..., datasets/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/emiliania_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=7eca0ef524dbb598...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-emiliania-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavelength from reaction and diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 gives f = a - u + u^2 v and g = b - u^2 v. | Henriksen et al. 2004: Emiliania CAP blocks acute calcite steps. Young & Henriksen 2003: coccolith calcite grows inside a vesicle.; reconstructed_in_script: a = 0.10, b = 0.90, D_v/D_u = 18 place k_c at 2 pi / 5.808 nm. | Predecessor lambda 7.744 nm is defined by six modes on the 46.464 nm patch. Successor delta is zero. | Shield spoke count 30 is the tangential-Sobel harmonic of this SEM, not a literature constant.; transfer_boundary: The CC BY-SA SEM is a micrometre-scale phenotype. The 5.808 nm field is mapped onto it. The photograph did not resolve 5.8 nm.; does_not_claim: That Emiliania forms pigment stripes or ocelli at 5.8 nm. | That 7.744 nm was measured on a fossil predecessor. | That CAP kinetics are Schnakenberg kinetics. | That one SEM is a population validation.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Closed. Tangential-Sobel annulus returns harmonic 30, spoke score 5.20, centre [192, 168], and that harmonic sets the shield.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Closed. wing_rmse = 0.0629 at dt = 0.006, stored beside the selection-band RMSE 0.0182. The wing error is still larger than the band error; it is reported rather than hidden.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.91e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

